# Leaves the copy the face HAL re-executes itself from.
#
# The HAL started from /vendor/bin/hw is in the linker class "vendor" and cannot
# load libgui.so, which only exists in /system/lib64. The same binary executed
# from under /data/local/tmp is in the class "unrestricted" and can. A ROM has
# nothing running script.sh at boot, and the HAL itself runs as `system`, which
# cannot write under /data/local/tmp (owned by shell), so init puts the copy
# there.
#
# The label is the part that needs help: a file created here would be
# shell_data_file and every exec of it would be denied. restorecon applies the
# entry that install_to_rom.sh appends to plat_file_contexts.
#
# post-fs-data, not late_start: the HAL starts in late_start and would race this
# action otherwise.
on post-fs-data
    # The parent is created by the platform's own post-fs-data action. If a ROM
    # creates it later than this file is parsed, the mkdir below fails with
    # ENOENT and nothing is copied, which shows up as "preview missing" with a
    # perfectly working HAL. Creating the parents first costs two lines and
    # removes the ordering assumption.
    mkdir /data/local 0771 root root
    mkdir /data/local/tmp 0771 shell shell
    mkdir /data/local/tmp/facehal 0775 system system
    copy /vendor/bin/hw/@HAL_NAME@ /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@
    chmod 0755 /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@
    chown system system /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@
    restorecon /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@
    copy /vendor/bin/hw/@HAL_NAME@ /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@.unrestr
    chmod 0755 /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@.unrestr
    chown system system /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@.unrestr
    restorecon /data/local/tmp/facehal/@HAL_NAME@.unrestr
